  "client_view_text": " A message that changes his life forever.\nThe lighthouse keeper, Jack, had been stationed on the rocky coast for five years. He had grown accustomed to the solitude, the rhythmic sound of the waves, and the occasional visit from a passing ship. But on this particular day, something caught his eye. A bottle, half-buried in the sand, caught the morning sun and glinted like a tiny jewel. Jack walked over to investigate, his boots sinking into the damp sand.\n\nAs he picked up the bottle, he noticed it was old, the glass worn and weathered. He carefully removed the cork and pulled out A message that changes his life forever.\nThe lighthouse keeper, Jack, had been stationed on the rocky coast for five years. He had grown accustomed to the solitude, the rhythmic sound of the waves, and the occasional visit from a passing ship. But on this particular day, something caught his eye. A bottle, half-buried in the sand, caught the morning sun and glinted like a tiny jewel. Jack walked towards it, curiosity getting the better of him.\n\nAs he picked up the bottle, he noticed it was old, the glass worn and weathered. He carefully removed the cork and pulled out a piece of paper, yellowed with age. Unfolding it, he saw that it was a letter, written in elegant script.\n\n\"Dear whoever finds this,\" the letter began, \"I am writing to you from the ship 'Eclipse', bound for the Americas. I am a young woman, traveling with my family to start a new life. We set sail from England in the spring of 1850, full of hope and dreams. But fate had other plans. A storm struck, and we were separated from our ship. I was washed overboard, and I have been clinging to this bottle ever since. I have no idea"
}